{
  "_comment": "The budget ledger (#1985). A READ-ONLY mirror of the budgets, one entry per budget: id, class, limit and where it is enforced. Classes: hard = never exceeded, takes no exception; release = ceiling is the last release measured + 5 percent, set only by `node scripts/set-ceilings.mjs --release` (in force since #1985 step 3); ratchet = moves down, or up only through an exception (what the audit zip and the Blazor analyzer budgets still are); advisory = reported, with only a backstop at 2x the old limit (8 KB per element), the figure that fails being the ledger limit, read from the `backstop` field of the budget (policy migration step 4, #1985). Blazor full is advisory too: its backstop is 2x the reference ceiling in packages.json, which set-ceilings --release still moves. The numbers are edited in their source (the file named in `source`); core/tests/budget-ledger.test.mjs fails when this file and the source disagree, so the ledger is never a second place to edit a number silently. `exceptions` holds approved BUDGET EXCEPTIONS: { budget, pr, approvedBy, reason }, added in the pull request that needs it and approved there by the owner or the orchestrating agent; no issue, plan or expiry. Hard gates take no exception, and neither does a release entry marked `noException: true` (page weight, the app entry, Blazor coreOnly). Release ceilings move only through scripts/set-ceilings.mjs --release. Entries with `movedBy` carry limit null: scripts/set-ceilings.mjs rewrites their source at the final gates, so the test reads the live value from the source instead of a copy that would go stale.",
